    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0484" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">768.75/6–446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in Albania</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State, at Paris</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-04T16:00:00+01:00">June 4, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 10—2:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>303. For Secdel for Dunn. Received this morning from Albanian Foreign Office note
                    dated June 3 signed Enver-Hoxa<anchor n="23" xml:id="d156-f1"/> in his various
                    capacities addressed Council Foreign Ministers charging Greece with having in
                    violation of all human principles driven into Albania in most destitute
                    circumstances about 23,000 Chams former residents northwestern Greece and
                    requesting that Council of Ministers take urgent measures: (1)Bring about their
                    repatriation; (2) arrange guarantees their civil, cultural and political rights;
                    (3) restitution or indemnification their property; (4) punishment responsible
                        persons.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d156-f2"/></p>
                <p>Note with my comments will be forwarded next plane scheduled here June 7.</p>
                <pb facs="0485" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>
                <p>Similar note handed French Chargé and assume also Soviet representative and
                    probably to British representative Belgrade.</p>
                <p>Sent Paris; repeated Dept 303.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacobs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="23" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>Enver Hoxha, Prime Minister and Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Albanian
                    regime.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d156-f2" n="24" xml:id="d156-f2-content">
                <p>The Albanian note under reference was subsequently sent to the Council of Foreign
                    Ministers through the French Embassy in Moscow. The note, which was circulated
                    to the Council as document C.F.M. (46) 142, June 25, 1946, not printed, was not
                    taken up by the Council. Additional documentation regarding the Greek-Albanian
                    dispute concerning the Chams is printed in <ref target="frus1946v07">volume <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
